      "writtenOn": "2024-10-17T23:50:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I like the readability of the current version:\n\n* It\u0027s shorter (less noise \u003d more signal from other lines of code)\n* It explicitly/directly asks to \"cast\" (rather than requiring the reader to understand that `SkTFitsIn` and `static_cast` are related\n\nAnd if we save a stack variable slot, then we have to call `fReader-\u003eget_actl_num_plays()` twice.  And if we don\u0027t call it twice, then we have to stash the result in a stack variable (e.g. `uint32_t ffiNumPlays \u003d ...`).\n\nAnd I haven\u0027t looked at the assembly, but I assume the compiler can potentially optimize away the \"ok\" bit.\u0027\n\nSo, let\u0027s just leave it as-is?",
